fpga-neural-predecoder
Copyright 2026 Nasir Ali, C-DAC Noida

This product is an independent, from-scratch implementation of a neural
pre-decoder concept for quantum error correction, targeting a Xilinx Alveo
U55C FPGA. It contains no source code from, and is not derived from, any
NVIDIA repository.

The method being reimplemented was originally published by NVIDIA in:

  - NVIDIA "Ising-Decoding" repository:
    https://github.com/NVIDIA/Ising-Decoding (Apache License 2.0)

  - Chamberland, Olle, Li, Thornton, Baratta, "Fast and accurate AI-based
    pre-decoders for surface codes", arXiv:2604.12841, 2026.

  - The companion color-code / Chromobius pre-decoder paper referenced
    alongside the above (color code is explicitly out of scope for this
    project).

No model weights, code, or other artifacts from the NVIDIA Ising-Decoding
repository or its associated Hugging Face checkpoints are included in or
were used to produce this repository. All neural network weights in this
project are trained locally, from scratch, on CPU.

This project depends on the following third-party open-source packages,
each under its own license (see requirements.txt for pinned versions):
Stim, PyMatching, NumPy, SciPy, PyTorch, Matplotlib, Pandas, pytest, PyYAML,
tqdm, and (host side, optional) pyxrt / Xilinx XRT.

